## Reviewed endpoint convention

Independent review (internal-review-repo `review/split-review.md`, revision 625be6641957282e695f21ca09fe958fe06fc51b) endorses the proposed split and likelihood standard. Float32 conversion can round a time to exactly 1200 s. Use NumPy histogram's last-bin inclusive-right convention: bins [0,1), ..., [1199,1200]. Record the number exactly at 1200 separately from genuine times >1200 or <0. All required photons remain accounted for. This quantization endpoint effect is negligible for parameter inference but must not silently lose observations. Review assignment request is resolved by the existing review/ allocation; final evidence remains pending.

## Presentation handoff compatibility

Figtab scripts at revision dd9f793e779d were offered under an alternative generator split, which is not adopted: release figures must also be computed by a non-generator, not only the report figure. Paper generation remains the requested allocation. Its acceptance is still pending. To use the existing figure renderer without translation, analysis will expose `results/fit.json` with `params.background_rate`, `params.burst_counts`, `params.centre`, `params.width`, each carrying `value` and `ci95` ([lower, upper]); explicit units, interval method, release provenance and diagnostics accompany these fields. `results/lightcurve.csv` will expose bin edges, observed counts, fitted integrated counts and residuals.

